WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.917 --> 00:00:03.712
♫ [MUSIC PLAYING] ♫ 

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:09.134
ROAR is an anthology series 

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.011
based on the short story collection 

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.887
"Roar" by Cecelia Ahern.

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:16.016
It's a series of eight stories 

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.852
that are essentially modern day feminist fables,

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:21.271
that takes the either a stereotype or

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.273
an issue that women face in society

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:26.401
and tells that story through a fun, surrealist lens.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.278
Get your little butt off of me!

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.654
Are you out of your damn mind?!

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:32.907
They put in front of people the things that

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:36.703
women are often meant to pretend they don't experience.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:41.541
If I am a ghost why am I still getting cramps?!

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.127
I love being able to highlight 

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:46.755
the different roles women play in our society, 

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.923
and their journeys to self-empowerment.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.468
We bounce from Betty Gilpin dancing

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.678
 in her own sort of manic musical,

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:57.140
to Cynthia Erivo telling a story of maternal guilt,

00:00:57.348 --> 00:00:59.642
to Nicole Kidman gobbling down photographs.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.854
It really is a sort of wild ride.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:07.650
The audience should expect the unexpected really.

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:10.153
Every single episode is so different,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.489
so wacky in a wonderful way.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.573
Are you okay?

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.908
I met someone.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:16.034
Oh my God!

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:21.081
Even though it's absurd and uh, sort of fantastical,

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.958
and magic realism, I think it's very very relatable.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:25.085
A mark!

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.966
What was really appealing about this project in particular

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:34.844
was the stories, cast, and the crew.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:36.346
They're very female centric.

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:39.766
It's amazing to work with so many females on set.

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:41.976
I feel so comfortable and free

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:45.021
It makes the experience different because

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:47.899
I don't know that I've ever laughed this much at work.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:50.527
It's certainly unlike anything I've ever done before.

00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:53.780
Sometimes we're trying to make you uncomfortable,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.074
sometimes we're trying to do the opposite,

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:57.909
but usually we want you to leave 

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.661
and carry the story with you for a while.

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:01.412
I mean it doesn't even look like a big potato,

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:02.539
it looks like a big turd.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:03.957
How stupid.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.751
Well it makes you smile, nothing's stupid about that.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:10.338
Hopefully women can see kind of, their roar,

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:13.049
their moment in every episode.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:14.551
That in some ways, 

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.803
you kind of can relate in different aspects 

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:18.304
to each of the leads,

00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:20.348
and each of the stories that is being told.

